exports[`AgentDirectoryHome · english copy golden master > no launches yet 1`] = `
[
  "TESTNET · BNB SMART CHAIN",
  "· Infinity",
  "The fair-launch",
  "terminal of the",
  "TQUOTE ecosystem.",
  "Currently staging on the public testnet.",
  "Fund a launch in TQUOTE — the same coin TapeOut circuits mine — through a window your gas history unlocks, then trade it on a 4,000-shelf price ladder. Every launch deploys its own PancakeSwap Infinity pool.",
  "Launch a token",
  "Project directory",
  "On-chain feed",
  "factory events",
  "No launches yet. The first one appears here the moment its factory event lands.",
  "Trending now",
  "Active markets",
  "View all",
  "Nothing is trading or raising yet",
  "The first launch appears here the moment its factory event lands. Until then, BNB Smart Chain Testnet has nothing open.",
  "Open the first launch",
  "// How it works",
  "How a Tosh launch works.",
  "Five steps, all settled on chain. Nothing here is enforced by this interface — the contract is the source of truth.",
  "01",
  "Quota",
  "Gas history sets your limit",
  "Gas is the one thing on chain nobody can manufacture: like the transistors burned at tape-out, once spent it never comes back. Tosh reads how much gas your wallet has genuinely burned and signs that into a deposit ceiling. A wallet minted this morning has no history to spend, so bot swarms have nothing to bring.",
  "02",
  "Launch",
  "Anyone can open one",
  "Pay the launch fee in tBNB and the token deploys together with its own PancakeSwap Infinity pool. No pre-mine, no team allocation, no supply held back for insiders.",
  "03",
  "Genesis",
  "A window that cannot close early",
  "Deposits run in TQUOTE for 3, 24 or 72 hours — the creator chooses once, at launch, and cannot shorten it afterwards. Every depositor takes back the full amount if the raise closes too small to open a pool, or if the creator never calls launch() inside the 7-day window after that.",
  "04",
  "Ladder",
  "Price climbs one shelf at a time",
  "After genesis the remaining supply is released across 4,000 fixed shelves spanning 2,000x from the opening price. A ceiling blocks spikes; 99% of what the shelves earn goes to the payout address the project names, and 1% to buy-and-burn.",
  "05",
  "Hardened",
  "The rules live in the contract; this page is a window",
  "Deposit accounting, the per-wallet deposit ceiling and the dust-deposit floor all live in the contract. This interface only mirrors them, so it cannot loosen them.",
]
`;

